# Herdr plugins to install, one per line: <plugin-id> <owner/repo[/subdir]> <ref>
#
# The id is the one the plugin declares in its herdr-plugin.toml; it is what
# `herdr plugin list` reports, so the sync needs it to tell installed from not.
#
# Applied by `herdr-plugins-sync`. Refs are pinned because Herdr has no
# `plugin update` — a reinstall is how a plugin moves forward, so bump the ref
# here and re-run the sync.
#
# Plugins are global to the user, not per-session, and are started by the Herdr
# *server*, so a newly installed plugin does nothing until `herdr server stop`
# (the session comes back with `herdr`).

chmarax.herdr-nvim  ChmaraX/herdr-nvim  v1.0.1
# Only real tag (rust-lite-v0.1.0) is a stale Lite-only checkpoint predating
# most current features (e.g. copy-archive); this plugin versions via internal
# .version-file bumps on main, not git tags, so we track main.
annotate  plannotator/herdr-annotate  main
